Since some of the Yukawa-dependent RGEs are quite lengthy, we provide them below, categorized by class, rather than including them in the main text. These expressions have been derived by applying Criterion I to the full set of RGEs.


\section{Class 3}

{


\noindent
\underline{\bf \boldmath $f^4 \to f^4$ (Yukawa)}:
\be
\begin{aligned}
\dotwc[(1)]{qq}{ijkl} & = y_b^2 \big(-\frac{1}{2} \delta_{k3} \delta_{l3} \wc[(1)]{qd}{ij33}-\frac{1}{8} \delta_{i3} \delta_{l3} \wc[(8)]{qd}{kj33}-\frac{1}{8} \delta_{j3} \delta_{k3} \wc[(8)]{qd}{il33} \\ 
&+\frac{1}{12} \delta_{k3} \delta_{l3} \wc[(8)]{qd}{ij33}+\frac{1}{2} \delta_{i3} \wc[(1)]{qq}{3jkl}+\frac{1}{2} \delta_{j3} \wc[(1)]{qq}{i3kl}+\frac{1}{2} \delta_{k3} \wc[(1)]{qq}{ij3l} \\ 
&+\frac{1}{2} \delta_{l3} \wc[(1)]{qq}{ijk3}\big)+y_t^2 \big(\frac{1}{2} V^*_{3i} V_{3v} \wc[(1)]{qq}{vjkl}+\frac{1}{2} V^*_{3k} V_{3v} \wc[(1)]{qq}{ijvl}+\frac{1}{2} V_{3j} V^*_{3v} \wc[(1)]{qq}{ivkl} \\ 
