\mathcal{W}^\prin(\calP_{\frac{p+2r}{q+2s}})\mathcal{W}^\prin(\calP_{\frac{p}{q}}) &= \mathcal{W}^\prin(\calP_{\frac{p+r}{q+s}})\bigg(\mathcal{W}^\prin(Q_3)  + \hat{y}_1^{d_1}\hat{y}_2^{d_2}\hat{y}_3^{d_3}\sqrt{\hat{Y}_{\frac{p}{q}}}\mathcal{W}^\prin(\calP_\frs)\bigg)\\
&+ \hat{y}_1^{2d_1}\hat{y}_2^{2d_2}\hat{y}_3^{2d_3}\hat{Y}_{\frac{p}{q}} \mathcal{W}^\prin(\calP_{\frac{r}{s}})^2
\end{align*}
where $Q_3$ is the poset on the same set as $Q_1$ but with $\calP_\fpq(\frac12 \cdot h_\fpq) > \calP_\fpq(\frac12 \cdot h_\fpq+1)$. We see that $Q_3$ is the same as $\overline{\calP_\frs} \searrow \overline{H} \searrow \overline{\calP_\fpq}$, i.e., $\calP_{\frac{p+r}{q+s}}$. As in the case with $d_\fpq$, we see that the degree vectors of the monomials in $\hat{y}_i$ match the $c$-vectors in Equation \eqref{eq:MutateGen}, and by induction we conclude $\mathcal{W}^\prin(\calP_{\frac{p+2r}{q+2s}}) = F_{\frac{p+2r}{q+2s}}$.

