under the null hypothesis, by using $\max_i \sigma_i^{*2}=O_p(1)$, $(\min_i(M_n)_{ii})^{-1}=O_p(1)$, 
$\max_{i} |\hat{\mu}_i(\beta_0) |/\sqrt{n} = o_p(1)$, 
and $n^{-1} \sum_{i=1}^n \hat{v}_i^4 = n^{-1} \sum_{i=1}^n (\tilde{Q}_i + \tilde{v}_i)^4 
