\section{Global Termination via Arithmetic Ranking} \label{sec:ranking}

To formally prove the convergence of the symbolic Collatz dynamics, we define a ranking function $\rho$ that decreases with each application of the transition function $T$. This function is based on the decimal structure of natural numbers and is primitive recursive.




\subsection{The Ranking Function}
To establish symbolic convergence of the Collatz dynamics, we define a ranking function $\rho(n)$ that serves as a strictly descending measure over finite segments of each trajectory. The function is constructed to reflect decimal structure and ensures progress towards termination.

For all $n \in \mathbb{N}_{>0}$, define:
\vspace{0.3em}
\begin{tcolorbox}[colback=gray!5!white, colframe=black!40, title= Ranking Function, sharp corners=south]
\[
\rho(n) := M \cdot \ell(n) + \text{digit\_sum}(n)
\]
\end{tcolorbox}


where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\ell(n) := \left\lfloor \log_{10}(n) \right\rfloor + 1$ is the number of decimal digits,
    \item $\mathrm{digit\_sum}(n) := \sum_{i=0}^{\ell(n)-1} r_i$ is the sum of digits of $n$ in base 10,
    \item and $M \in \mathbb{N}$ is a fixed constant with $M > 9$.
\end{itemize}

