    \field{abstract}{%
    We present a simple method to produce giant lipid pseudo-vesicles (vesicles
  with an oily cap on the top), trapped in an agarose gel. The method can be
  implemented using only a regular micropipette and relies on the formation of
  a water/oil/water double droplet in liquid agarose. We characterize the
  produced vesicle with fluorescence imaging and establish the presence and
  integrity of the lipid bilayer by the successful insertion of $$\alpha $$
  -Hemolysin transmembrane proteins. Finally, we show that the vesicle can be
  easily mechanically deformed, non-intrusively, by indenting the surface of
  the gel.%
