    \field{abstract}{%
    The differentiation of pluripotent stem cells in three-dimensional cultures
  can recapitulate key aspects of brain development, but protocols are prone to
  variable results. Here we differentiated multiple human pluripotent stem cell
  lines for over 100 d using our previously developed approach to generate
  brain-region-specific organoids called cortical spheroids and, using several
  assays, found that spheroid generation was highly reliable and consistent. We
  anticipate the use of this approach for large-scale differentiation
  experiments and disease modeling.%
