In~\Cref{thm:contbij2Ninfty}, one can build a continuous bijection from two
such continuous injections $f, g$ of the same type by usual Cantor-Bernstein-style
arguments. For the other cases, it is useful to note that if both $f$ and $g$
are tangled, then $f \circ g$ is untangled and still a continuous injection.
}
