            1 & \z_{2, 1} & \z_{2, 2} & \z_{2, 1}^2 & \z_{2, 1}\z_{2, 2} & \z_{2, 2}^2\\
            1 & \z_{3, 1} & \z_{3, 2} & \z_{3, 1}^2 & \z_{3, 1}\z_{3, 2} & \z_{3, 2}^2\\
            1 & \z_{4, 1} & \z_{4, 2} & \z_{4, 1}^2 & \z_{4, 1}\z_{4, 2} & \z_{4, 2}^2
        \end{bmatrix},\]
        we can expand both $m\cdot m_{x_1^2}^{x_2^2}$ and $\bb{m_{x_1^2}^{x_1x_2}}^2$ as polynomials in the $\z_{i, j}$ and find monomials that appear in one but not the other.  For example, one such monomial that appears in $m\cdot m_{x_1^2}^{x_2^2}$ but not $\bb{m_{x_1^2}^{x_1x_2}}^2$ (up to sign) is 
