\subsubsection{DaCe, the Data-Centric Programming Framework} In this work, we use the DaCe \cite{dace} framework to generate optimized code to be integrated into the CFD code. DaCe programming framework is actively developed at ETH Zürich and has several publications and applications. The DaCe includes a restricted Python interface that allows the programmers to express the scientific code. The most famous application wholly developed in DaCe is the OMEN code for material science studies. The OMEN code was awarded the prestigious Gordon Bell Award for enabling full-machine Summit simulations. The DaCe framework is based on an Intermediate Representation (IR) called SDFG which is designed to express data flow and portability of parallelism. The IR is generated from a high-level python front-end and generates a graphical graph representation of the program. 

