%In the previous proof, we can say a bit more: by using the fact that the restriction map $\rho_L: \FA(G)\to\FA(L)$ is contractive, one can show that
%\[
%\norm{J^{-1}\iota_\Delta :\FA(G)\to\FA(G)\ptp\FA(G)}
%=
%\norm{J^{-1}\iota_\Delta :\FA(L)\to\FA(L)\ptp\FA(L)} \,.
%\]
% This is in the same spirit as the result that for any virtually abelian group $G$ there is a countable subgroup $\Gamma\leq G$ such that $\AD(G)=\AD(\Gamma)$ (see \cite[Lemma 2.7]{Choi-minorant}). 
% Similar ideas can be seen in Theorem \ref{t:AMA-discrete-countable} and its proof.
