\section{CONCLUSIONS}

We present a high order collaboration-oriented federated graph neural network for accurate QoS prediction, referred to as HC-FGNN. This method enables similarity assessment on the server side based on user-uploaded feature information, allowing for the selection of the top-\textit{k} most similar users as neighbor information. This approach provides higher-order user information at the client side, rather than relying solely on individual client information. Our approach effectively preserves user data privacy while ensuring prediction accuracy. Extensive experiments demonstrate that our proposed HC-FGNN framework achieves commendable performance, and we hope to apply this model to other collaborative recommendation systems, yielding positive outcomes.
