To compare the lyrical content preservation capabilities of the proposed model and the baseline, we extracted Hindi content embeddings using IndicWav2Vec from LAPS-Diff, DiffSinger, and the ground truth audio. These high-dimensional embeddings are projected onto a 2D space using Principal Component Analysis (PCA) \cite{PCA} for visualization. As illustrated in Fig. \ref{Fig-2:PCA}, the LAPS-Diff embeddings are located closer to the ground truth than those from DiffSinger, indicating that LAPS-Diff captures content information more effectively.
