\subsubsection{Conclusion on Arbitrage Opportunities}
These results suggest that during periods of high network activity, such as March 5th, 2024, arbitrage opportunities are scarce due to elevated gas fees. Our analysis shows that even when price divergences occur, the cost of executing trades on the Ethereum network effectively cancels out any potential profit. It is also important to note that we have not accounted for slippage, which would further reduce the profitability of such strategies. In conclusion, arbitrage opportunities in the Ethereum market for ETH are difficult to exploit in high-fee environments.
