\medskip
To summarize, here we have shown that, in order to maximize the LWFA of the first  self-injected electrons (FSIE) in the PW induced by a given laser pulse at the downramp: i) the plateau level $\bar{n}$ has to be chosen as the unique value $\bar{n}_j=\nu_j\, n_{cr}$ associated to the pulse (section \ref{WFA.b}); ii) with the present level of approximation, and assuming a linear downramp for simplicity, the pair of %average 
parameters ($n_b,\delta Z$) featuring the downramp has to be chosen in the set (broken line) $\Lambda$  (section \ref{WFA.c}); iii) there is a large freedom in choosing the upramp so that it does not affect the WFA of the FSIE  (section \ref{WFA.d}). The procedure is very promising and deserves further investigations  in view of improvements and possible developments. We believe that a more refined tailoring of the downramp would yield a much more peaked energy spectrum of the self-injected electrons already at the early stages of their LWFA.







