Another frequently used two qubit operator is the $\swapop$ gate, which operates by swapping the states of two qubits:
\begin{equation}
    \swapop(\ket{\psi}\ket{\phi})=\ket{\phi}\ket{\psi}.
\end{equation}
It can be shown that any permutation of $k$ things can be written as a composition
of transpositions (the swap permutation). Thus, on the Hilbert space level, we
can perform a permutation of arbitrarily many states by combining swap operators.
The circuit notation for the $\swapop$ gate is shown in Figure~\ref{fig:swap}.

